WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.306 --> 00:00:03.158
- To those who can overcome the obstacles,

00:00:03.158 --> 00:00:05.825
rise up when difficulties arise,

00:00:07.545 --> 00:00:09.125
are the ones who win the prize.

00:00:09.125 --> 00:00:12.265
Everybody starts at the bottom

00:00:12.265 --> 00:00:14.284
and there is no advantage
to starting 10 years ago,

00:00:14.284 --> 00:00:15.506
as opposed to starting today.

00:00:15.506 --> 00:00:16.968
In fact, it's better
today, than it was then.

00:00:16.968 --> 00:00:20.051
Action is determined by your attitude

00:00:21.579 --> 00:00:25.674
and attitude is determined by your acts.

00:00:25.674 --> 00:00:28.653
- He's an American
businessman, cofounder of Amway

00:00:28.653 --> 00:00:31.167
and owner of the Orlando
Magic basketball team.

00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:34.321
At one point, he was one of
the 10 wealthiest Americans.

00:00:34.321 --> 00:00:35.454
He has an estimated net worth

00:00:35.454 --> 00:00:37.923
of five point one billion dollars.

00:00:37.923 --> 00:00:39.045
He's Rich DeVos

00:00:39.045 --> 00:00:41.628
and here's my take on his
top 10 rules to success.

00:00:41.628 --> 00:00:43.481
Rule number five is my personal favorite

00:00:43.481 --> 00:00:45.885
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:45.885 --> 00:00:47.412
And as always guys, if hear something

00:00:47.412 --> 00:00:48.749
that really resonates with you,

00:00:48.749 --> 00:00:50.388
please leave it down the comments below.

00:00:50.388 --> 00:00:51.719
Put quotes around that as well,

00:00:51.719 --> 00:00:53.508
so other people can be inspired.

00:00:53.508 --> 00:00:55.392
Also, when you write it
down, you're much more likely

00:00:55.392 --> 00:00:58.059
to lock in for yourself as well.

00:00:58.059 --> 00:00:58.892
Enjoy.

00:01:01.784 --> 00:01:04.451
(soaring music)

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:13.569
- You are a part of something

00:01:13.569 --> 00:01:17.741
that transcends all the
details of your business.

00:01:17.741 --> 00:01:21.878
It's a part of demonstrating
that free enterprise works,

00:01:21.878 --> 00:01:24.992
that someone can start
with a $50 sales kit

00:01:24.992 --> 00:01:27.997
and build a large business.

00:01:27.997 --> 00:01:31.570
You prove it every day that it works

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:35.016
and you prove it by
overcoming the obstacles

00:01:35.016 --> 00:01:37.536
that you have to deal with.

00:01:37.536 --> 00:01:39.841
There are all sorts of people
that want to break your faith.

00:01:39.841 --> 00:01:42.008
Some enter your own family

00:01:43.777 --> 00:01:46.054
and sometimes they're just
so-called good friends,

00:01:46.054 --> 00:01:49.931
who think you're crazy for
doing what you're doing.

00:01:49.931 --> 00:01:54.883
But you see, you have decided
to take charge of your life.

00:01:54.883 --> 00:01:57.866
You have decided that you
are going to change it.

00:01:57.866 --> 00:01:59.285
You're not going to
wait for the government,

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:00.920
you're not going to wait for some school

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.515
or something else to happen.

00:02:02.515 --> 00:02:05.765
You are going to change your situation.

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:10.157
That's what free enterprise is all about.

00:02:10.157 --> 00:02:12.586
Jay and I decided to do that,

00:02:12.586 --> 00:02:16.093
I don't know over 50, 60 years ago.

00:02:16.093 --> 00:02:19.760
We started in this kind
of business in 1949.

00:02:20.597 --> 00:02:21.430
I was 23.

00:02:23.118 --> 00:02:25.757
All I know is this business.

00:02:25.757 --> 00:02:27.590
I spent my life at it,

00:02:28.454 --> 00:02:29.871
went pretty good,

00:02:31.075 --> 00:02:33.358
but it wasn't always easy.

00:02:33.358 --> 00:02:36.040
Business isn't, life isn't,

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:38.894
but to those who can
overcome the obstacles,

00:02:38.894 --> 00:02:41.561
rise up when difficulties arise,

00:02:43.114 --> 00:02:45.533
are the ones who win the prize.

00:02:45.533 --> 00:02:48.078
I recently picked up a book

00:02:48.078 --> 00:02:52.245
by a Dr. Norman Doidge, D-O-I-D-G-E.

00:02:54.718 --> 00:02:56.901
He's a brain guy.

00:02:56.901 --> 00:02:57.984
Psychiatrist.

00:02:59.357 --> 00:03:03.941
And his study says that I
can confirm to you the power

00:03:03.941 --> 00:03:06.858
of positive thinking scientifically

00:03:08.494 --> 00:03:11.351
because so many people ridicule

00:03:11.351 --> 00:03:13.210
that whole idea of positive thinking.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:16.055
I can show you positively,

00:03:16.055 --> 00:03:18.054
that turning yourself

00:03:18.054 --> 00:03:20.112
into a positive thinker
will change your brain

00:03:20.112 --> 00:03:22.005
and how it functions and
how you think about yourself

00:03:22.005 --> 00:03:24.048
and what you can accomplish.

00:03:24.048 --> 00:03:28.146
Now it's been laughed
at and most of my life

00:03:28.146 --> 00:03:32.313
and people say, oh that,
that's just wishful thinking.

00:03:33.189 --> 00:03:35.117
Well, I don't think it's wishful thinking,

00:03:35.117 --> 00:03:37.312
Norman didn't think it
was wishful thinking.

00:03:37.312 --> 00:03:39.899
His was all biblically based

00:03:39.899 --> 00:03:43.316
and Bob Schuller did pretty good with it.

00:03:44.573 --> 00:03:45.406
I did pretty good with it.

00:03:45.406 --> 00:03:49.843
Starting at the bottom at Amway
is where ever you are today.

00:03:49.843 --> 00:03:52.831
Everybody starts at the bottom

00:03:52.831 --> 00:03:54.673
and there is no advantage
to starting 10 years ago,

00:03:54.673 --> 00:03:55.930
as opposed to starting today.

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:58.269
In fact it's better
today than it was then.

00:03:58.269 --> 00:03:59.733
Our products are better,
our line is better,

00:03:59.733 --> 00:04:02.176
our plant is better, it's more proven.

00:04:02.176 --> 00:04:06.009
It's a better plan today
than when we started.

00:04:07.027 --> 00:04:08.422
And sometimes there are no answers

00:04:08.422 --> 00:04:09.734
as to whether you want to be in business

00:04:09.734 --> 00:04:10.868
or would like to be in business.

00:04:10.868 --> 00:04:13.271
You just got to put year
toe in the water, you know.

00:04:13.271 --> 00:04:15.074
If your going to wait
until you know everything,

00:04:15.074 --> 00:04:17.157
you'll never do anything.

00:04:19.782 --> 00:04:21.490
And you'll always say, well
I got to check some more,

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:22.536
I'm going to and a little more research.

00:04:22.536 --> 00:04:24.426
So go ahead, just keep going

00:04:24.426 --> 00:04:27.011
and you'll never get in a business.

00:04:27.011 --> 00:04:30.264
You're going to go swimming,
you got to get wet, you know.

00:04:30.264 --> 00:04:32.171
And then you find the
people that got a hot button

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:34.531
for having a business of their own

00:04:34.531 --> 00:04:35.587
and want to do their own thing

00:04:35.587 --> 00:04:39.359
and like the chance to
build a big business.

00:04:39.359 --> 00:04:41.250
Well, you got to have that dream.

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:42.991
That's why other people
talk about having a dream.

00:04:42.991 --> 00:04:46.168
Hell, you got to have a
little bit of a dream.

00:04:46.168 --> 00:04:47.312
And then you say, I'll
go out and get customers,

00:04:47.312 --> 00:04:50.453
you know I got a chance to
really build a big thing.

00:04:50.453 --> 00:04:51.880
I'm going to go out
and get some customers.

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:54.892
When you start something
new it's not easy,

00:04:54.892 --> 00:04:56.692
but life is easier when you got a business

00:04:56.692 --> 00:05:01.283
and you're making some money,
makes it a little easier.

00:05:01.283 --> 00:05:02.858
So, stick with it,

00:05:02.858 --> 00:05:05.018
find a way through it,
just find out an answer.

00:05:05.018 --> 00:05:07.535
It works folks, this business works

00:05:07.535 --> 00:05:08.619
for those who work it.

00:05:08.619 --> 00:05:11.718
Now, I want to spend a little time

00:05:11.718 --> 00:05:13.956
on a kind of an old subject

00:05:13.956 --> 00:05:17.238
and yet it's new in some ways,

00:05:17.238 --> 00:05:19.405
but it deals with the fear

00:05:21.411 --> 00:05:24.793
of failure that affects all of us.

00:05:24.793 --> 00:05:27.839
And I know you've come here with hopes

00:05:27.839 --> 00:05:31.197
and faith in your future, but
back there is a little bit

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:34.807
of fear about whether you can do it

00:05:34.807 --> 00:05:37.807
or what somebody will say about you.

00:05:38.768 --> 00:05:42.193
Sometimes we have people
come to a meeting like this,

00:05:42.193 --> 00:05:44.222
who are even afraid to tell their friends

00:05:44.222 --> 00:05:46.414
they came to an Amway meeting for fear

00:05:46.414 --> 00:05:48.143
of what they will say.

00:05:48.143 --> 00:05:51.318
And so we are so driven by fear

00:05:51.318 --> 00:05:55.530
that sometimes we never do
anything because we're a fear

00:05:55.530 --> 00:05:57.860
of what somebody else will say.

00:05:57.860 --> 00:06:02.753
And what happens when you
do that is you give control

00:06:02.753 --> 00:06:06.399
of your life over to someone else.

00:06:06.399 --> 00:06:11.106
And then they decide what's
going to happen to you,

00:06:11.106 --> 00:06:13.197
instead of you deciding.

00:06:13.197 --> 00:06:15.843
Now we have the fear of failure,

00:06:15.843 --> 00:06:18.010
the fear of what other people will say,

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:21.510
the fear of rejection, the fear of change.

00:06:23.057 --> 00:06:26.559
Now the first thing we
must do is deal with change

00:06:26.559 --> 00:06:31.223
and learn to accept the fact
that things are changing fast

00:06:31.223 --> 00:06:34.571
and so to illustrate how to handle change,

00:06:34.571 --> 00:06:37.973
I thought since I hadn't
been here in eight years,

00:06:37.973 --> 00:06:40.891
I would give you a little Amway history,

00:06:40.891 --> 00:06:44.141
so you would see how we handled change.

00:06:45.214 --> 00:06:48.434
When Jay Van Andel and I
started our first business,

00:06:48.434 --> 00:06:51.132
we started a flying school.

00:06:51.132 --> 00:06:53.057
Now that was a change,

00:06:53.057 --> 00:06:54.468
but the important thing is

00:06:54.468 --> 00:06:57.680
that neither one of us knew how to fly

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:00.672
and so when you consider
doing something new,

00:07:00.672 --> 00:07:04.531
you say, oh, I can't do
it, I've never done this.

00:07:04.531 --> 00:07:08.490
We didn't let our not flying
stop us from starting.

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:10.922
We just began and hired instructors

00:07:10.922 --> 00:07:12.898
and learned from them.

00:07:12.898 --> 00:07:15.916
Actually what it finally
comes down to in your business

00:07:15.916 --> 00:07:19.833
and how you run it, is
you first and me second.

00:07:21.657 --> 00:07:25.669
Take that home with you,
you first and me second.

00:07:25.669 --> 00:07:28.536
The first thing you want to
do is help your people succeed

00:07:28.536 --> 00:07:30.177
and then you succeed.

00:07:30.177 --> 00:07:32.189
Just keep it in the right order.

00:07:32.189 --> 00:07:33.227
It's not you succeeding

00:07:33.227 --> 00:07:36.343
and then hopefully they come out okay.

00:07:36.343 --> 00:07:39.785
It's all about them, not about you

00:07:39.785 --> 00:07:42.695
and I think that was the
foundation of our business.

00:07:42.695 --> 00:07:45.496
You know we never, Jay and I never talked

00:07:45.496 --> 00:07:46.935
about how much money we made

00:07:46.935 --> 00:07:49.505
or how much money we wanted to make.

00:07:49.505 --> 00:07:52.374
We talked about how big we'd
like to have our business,

00:07:52.374 --> 00:07:56.686
but it was never a
personal financial goal.

00:07:56.686 --> 00:07:59.661
But our focus was on how
we could enrich the lives

00:07:59.661 --> 00:08:02.931
of our people and make them better,

00:08:02.931 --> 00:08:05.976
often times influencing
them with our faith as well.

00:08:05.976 --> 00:08:08.809
My father was a very positive guy.

00:08:09.645 --> 00:08:12.010
You know, you can do it, you
can do it, you can do it.

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:13.510
That was his mind.

00:08:15.107 --> 00:08:18.688
And I was like, you know,
people say, oh I can't do that.

00:08:18.688 --> 00:08:21.594
He was the one who said yes you can.

00:08:21.594 --> 00:08:25.677
He wouldn't accept from
me a no or I can't do it.

00:08:27.561 --> 00:08:31.943
He would get on me hard
about even saying it,

00:08:31.943 --> 00:08:33.383
even thinking you can't do it.

00:08:33.383 --> 00:08:36.633
I graduated as class president finally.

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:40.902
So I had to speak at the commencement

00:08:40.902 --> 00:08:44.790
and he helped me put my speech together.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:47.724
It turned out to be pretty good.

00:08:47.724 --> 00:08:48.660
One morning he came up to me

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:50.905
and said, you know you
were a lot better than

00:08:50.905 --> 00:08:55.383
that minister we had who
was our guest speaker.

00:08:55.383 --> 00:08:56.804
That little phrase,

00:08:56.804 --> 00:08:59.470
that little experience
really encouraged me

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:03.108
to keep at it, on the speaking side.

00:09:03.108 --> 00:09:06.257
His encouragement to me led me

00:09:06.257 --> 00:09:10.084
to build a life around encouraging others.

00:09:10.084 --> 00:09:11.636
And so, that's where I've done.

00:09:11.636 --> 00:09:13.219
Attitude and action

00:09:15.261 --> 00:09:16.639
and atmosphere.

00:09:16.639 --> 00:09:20.365
You want to take the correct action.

00:09:20.365 --> 00:09:23.532
Action is determined by your attitude.

00:09:24.903 --> 00:09:28.679
And attitude is determined
by your atmosphere.

00:09:28.679 --> 00:09:31.888
Always put yourself in an atmosphere

00:09:31.888 --> 00:09:35.341
where you have a chance to succeed.

00:09:35.341 --> 00:09:39.410
Put yourself in the presence
of people who think like you,

00:09:39.410 --> 00:09:43.327
who want to get ahead
like you and lift you up.

00:09:44.321 --> 00:09:47.395
So not only am I encouraging
use phrases of up,

00:09:47.395 --> 00:09:51.562
phrases up encouragement,
but to be an encourager,

00:09:52.523 --> 00:09:55.598
but to hang around with
people who do that.

00:09:55.598 --> 00:09:57.847
And when you deal with your people

00:09:57.847 --> 00:09:59.591
and you bring a new one in,

00:09:59.591 --> 00:10:01.999
it's their success you need

00:10:01.999 --> 00:10:04.082
and then you get rewards.

00:10:05.113 --> 00:10:07.429
That's why people want to
take a lot of money out

00:10:07.429 --> 00:10:10.058
of the sales kit and it's
against the law, first of all,

00:10:10.058 --> 00:10:11.810
to do that as part of our settlement

00:10:11.810 --> 00:10:13.692
with the government here,

00:10:13.692 --> 00:10:16.661
that we would not put money
in the sales kit as a profit.

00:10:16.661 --> 00:10:18.982
So there's no profit in
the act of recruiting.

00:10:18.982 --> 00:10:23.411
The profit comes when you
help that person succeed.

00:10:23.411 --> 00:10:26.959
That's a vital foundation principle.

00:10:26.959 --> 00:10:28.376
Help others first

00:10:29.595 --> 00:10:31.766
and then you succeed.

00:10:31.766 --> 00:10:35.933
It's been a long time since
I told stories about my boat,

00:10:37.427 --> 00:10:41.554
but Jay and I bought a schooner,
the schooner Elizabeth.

00:10:41.554 --> 00:10:43.300
And this is the bell off from it

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:46.841
and it's only important
because the boat sank.

00:10:46.841 --> 00:10:50.689
She was kind of a nice little
boat, but she leaked a lot.

00:10:50.689 --> 00:10:54.047
That was our first big
sailing experiences,

00:10:54.047 --> 00:10:55.782
but we bought it, we went on it, we sank

00:10:55.782 --> 00:10:58.683
and have owned many boats since then.

00:10:58.683 --> 00:11:00.434
You learn from mistakes.

00:11:00.434 --> 00:11:03.008
You got to start with faith
and belief in yourself.

00:11:03.008 --> 00:11:06.048
That's something you got to
make it your business to do.

00:11:06.048 --> 00:11:10.607
It's from the heart that
we derive our emotions

00:11:10.607 --> 00:11:14.774
and our energy to take on
and meet new challenges.

00:11:18.001 --> 00:11:19.584
This is a business,

00:11:20.865 --> 00:11:23.899
where your heart has to be in it

00:11:23.899 --> 00:11:28.049
and you have to believe
that you can do it.

00:11:28.049 --> 00:11:32.421
And overcome the resistance
and the negative influence

00:11:32.421 --> 00:11:34.588
of others to move forward.

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:38.451
So have a good heart for this business.

00:11:38.451 --> 00:11:40.961
And find out what you can do,

00:11:40.961 --> 00:11:43.894
most all of you will
discover you can do things

00:11:43.894 --> 00:11:46.019
you never thought you could do.

00:11:46.019 --> 00:11:48.364
You can advance farther
than you ever thought

00:11:48.364 --> 00:11:51.230
you could advance once you put your heart

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:54.313
into believing that you can do that.

00:11:56.114 --> 00:11:57.681
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:11:57.681 --> 00:12:00.193
I made this video because
Kris Westcott asked me to,

00:12:00.193 --> 00:12:02.119
so if there's a famous
entrepreneur that you want me

00:12:02.119 --> 00:12:04.187
to profile next, leave it
down in the comments below

00:12:04.187 --> 00:12:05.341
and I'll see what I can do.

00:12:05.341 --> 00:12:07.017
I'd also love to know what did Rich say

00:12:07.017 --> 00:12:08.698
that had the biggest impact on you.

00:12:08.698 --> 00:12:10.264
What are you going to take from this video

00:12:10.264 --> 00:12:12.803
and immediately apply to your
life, your business somehow?

00:12:12.803 --> 00:12:14.275
Leave it down in the comments below

00:12:14.275 --> 00:12:15.959
and I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:12:15.959 --> 00:12:17.289
Finally, I wanted to
give a quick shout out

00:12:17.289 --> 00:12:19.550
to Bitesize Lessons by Mr. Mo.

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:21.555
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:12:21.555 --> 00:12:24.342
Your One Word and making
that awesome cartoon

00:12:24.342 --> 00:12:26.252
and posting it to your Instagram page.

00:12:26.252 --> 00:12:27.744
I really, really, really appreciate it

00:12:27.744 --> 00:12:28.753
and hope you're enjoying the book.

00:12:28.753 --> 00:12:30.274
So, thank you guys again for watching.

00:12:30.274 --> 00:12:31.701
I believe in you.

00:12:31.701 --> 00:12:33.829
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:12:33.829 --> 00:12:35.363
and whatever your one word is,

00:12:35.363 --> 00:12:37.780
much love, I'll see you soon.

00:12:44.658 --> 00:12:46.094
- Keep, keep it on, keep on.

00:12:46.094 --> 00:12:46.927
- Yeah.

00:12:46.927 --> 00:12:47.812
- That's all.

00:12:47.812 --> 00:12:50.041
There's always tough
periods in any business,

00:12:50.041 --> 00:12:52.041
in any life, in any time

00:12:53.631 --> 00:12:55.672
and that doesn't mean anything,

00:12:55.672 --> 00:12:57.363
except you got to work your way around it

00:12:57.363 --> 00:12:59.780
and work your way through it.

00:13:00.725 --> 00:13:01.842
It doesn't say.

00:13:01.842 --> 00:13:03.196
You review your plan,

00:13:03.196 --> 00:13:05.615
figure out what you might
have done right or different

00:13:05.615 --> 00:13:07.615
and then get on with it.

00:13:08.527 --> 00:13:12.694
If everybody quit when things
were not quite favorable,

00:13:14.108 --> 00:13:16.370
well, then would nobody
would get anywhere,

00:13:16.370 --> 00:13:18.588
but if you want to get somewhere,

00:13:18.588 --> 00:13:20.452
the best time is when it's bad.

00:13:20.452 --> 00:13:22.928
So that while everybody else is trying,

00:13:22.928 --> 00:13:24.594
you're working

00:13:24.594 --> 00:13:25.427
(audience laughing)

00:13:25.427 --> 00:13:27.346
and you've done your business.

00:13:27.346 --> 00:13:28.179
(audience applauding)

00:13:28.179 --> 00:13:30.094
- [Host] Thank you very much, Rich DeVos.

